<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996 grain output estimated by type - CNA.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996 grain output estimated by type - CNA.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimates for Mexican grain and oilseed output for 1996 were released by the National Farm Council (CNA) on Wednesday with comparisons for 1995. Figures in tonnes.</p>
<p>    Product			 1996		  1995</p>
<p>Grains</p>
<p>    Corn			 17,980,400	   18,352,856</p>
<p>    Wheat			 3,322,600	    3,468,217</p>
<p>    Rice			    374,000		367,030</p>
<p>    Dry beans		   1,325,400	    1,270,915</p>
<p>Oilseeds</p>
<p>    Sesame			   48,900		 21,081</p>
<p>    Cotton			  367,030		433,200</p>
<p>    Safflower		     181,600		113,267</p>
<p>    Soybean			  90,600		189,774</p>
<p>Other Grains</p>
<p>    Barley			  544,700		486,636</p>
<p>    Sorghum		     5,866,100	    4,169,898</p>
<p>    Total Grains	     29,413,200	   28,115,552</p>
<p>    Total Oilseeds		754,300		691,152</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
</text>
